# What:  the settings each person needs on their own machine. This file is a template (committed, no real values).
# How:   copy it to .env.local (git-ignored, never committed) and fill in the values from the team chat.
#        Claude is not allowed to read .env.local, and real addresses must never be written in the repo.
# Related: .claude/rules/api-backend-access-security.md, .claude/docs/backend-services-list.md

# ── Backend ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The API gateway: ONE address in front of all 6 Spring Boot services (user, project, provisioning,
# ai-codegen, payment, notification). Server-only — never rename it to NEXT_PUBLIC_*.
# Only the Next.js server talks to it (the backend has no CORS). No trailing slash.
BACKEND_API_URL=

# ── Call diary (development only) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Your short name (e.g. your first name). Real API results you get while testing are saved to
# api-status/<name>.json, which keeps API_TRACKING.md up to date. Leave empty to record nothing.
API_STATUS_NAME=
